  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding of Alaska Medicaid Opzelura (ruxolitinib), effective 2022-11-01. Closed indications attest to mild to moderate AD or nonsegmental vitiligo.",
    "Source wording preserved: AD up to 20% BSA; vitiligo states 10% BSA without an inequality. The vitiligo attestation is literal; interpretation as a maximum requires manual review.",
    "The source overlaps corticosteroid age bands: age ≤17 low-mid potency and age ≥17 high potency. Both classes are required at exactly age 17; trial/failure or contraindication qualifies independently for each. Outside that overlap only the age-applicable class is required.",
    "Cautions (notes only): serious bacterial, mycobacterial, fungal and viral infections; monitor and manage promptly. Basal cell and squamous cell skin cancers: periodic skin examinations. Cytopenias (thrombocytopenia, anemia, neutropenia): CBC monitoring as indicated. Thrombosis (DVT, pulmonary embolism, arterial thrombosis) and major adverse cardiac events (MACE).",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval up to 2 months; reauthorization up to 1 year with disease improvement and/or stabilization and no serious adverse effects.",
    "Quantity (notes only): 4 × 60gm tubes per 28 days (60gm per 7 days); source also lists 2 × 100gm tubes per 28 days (100gm per 14 days).",
    "Remaining gaps: cautions, monitoring, duration, reauthorization, quantity enforcement and BSA wording interpretation require manual review. PDL status unknown; source is silent."
  ],
